well with german germany struggling to  contain a massive surge in covert 19  infections talk of a vaccine mandate is  heating up in the coming weeks the new  parliament will vote on whether to  require all residents to get the jab in  the meantime germany's federal and state  leaders have decreed that care home  workers must get vaccinated but there  are concerns that the measure could lead  to serious staffing shortages if they  react by quitting their jobs  matthias postman has been working as a  geriatric nurse for 12 years  he supports the decision to introduce  mandatory vaccination for care workers  to keep the risk of infection as low as  possible for everyone here  you feel safer knowing for certain that  all of your colleagues all the people  you work with are vaccinated  and that there are no ifs and butts on  that front  vaccine hesitancy or even refusal has  proven a pervasive problem in germany's  care home sector  how pervasive no one knows that's why  andrea yeager welcomes the mandates but  she says they shouldn't be limited to  nurses  i would like to see the government move  more swiftly to introduce a general  nationwide vaccine requirement instead  of just focusing on the sectors that are  already under pressure  i don't like the message the sends or  the pressure this puts on nurses you  must get vaccinated while essentially  telling everyone else that they can take  their sweet time because they're not as  likely to drive up infections  a national mandate is under debate but  it wouldn't go into effect until  february in the meantime to protect the  particularly vulnerable the government  is now eyeing a targeted mandate for all  nursing home staff a move welcomed by  many in the business  you can't just single out any one group  or industry because there's no way of  knowing if they're the ones responsible  there are so many people involved in  running a nursing home from housekeeping  to the janitor from care attendance to  those who work in administration and  often enter patients rooms  [Music]  but some worry that the mix of covered  19 staff shortages and vaccine  requirements are placing too big a  burden on workers already stretched to  their limits  those who are still left to shoulder  this undue burden are being put under  even more pressure and i worry that this  could be the last straw that they'll go  i can't i won't do this anymore and quit  for nurse matthias busman though vaccine  mandates are the only way to get out of  this crisis first for care homes and  hospitals then for the rest of the  country  i say vaccinate anyone and everyone as  fast as humanly possible  [Music]  let's talk now to andrew allman he's a  member of the german parliament for the  fdp and a doctor with expertise in  infectious diseases dr ulman how  concerned are you that the mandatory  vaccination will cause people in the  nursing field to quit their jobs  honestly i'm not too concerned if we  look into other countries in europe like  for example france or  united kingdom we do see some people  leaving their job but on the other hand  most of the people stay there and stay  put and it's obvious that we have an  issue there however i think it's very  important and shows some kind of  responsibility  if we get the vaccine mandate out there  in the institutions and again it's not  the nursing staff per se it's all the  staff who are working in an institution  now the buddhist target is set to debate  a vote on a nationwide vaccination  mandate how sure are you that there will  be a majority for it in parliament  well the first step we're starting this  week in parliament is mandatory  vaccination institution for institutions  like hospitals or nursing care or a  private practice  that has to be first implemented and the  next steps are being debated right now  internally how far we will go with the  mandate of vaccination for the whole  population or special groups in our  population for example the elderly or  the adults  your party the fdp has for a long time  promised that there'll be no mandatory  vaccination nationwide  many people who voted for you now say  they feel betrayed others are worried  that the divisions in society will get  even deeper what do you say to them  well the truth is all parties  said they do not want to have vaccine  mandates or mandatory vaccination i said  the same thing by the way even during  the campaigning i said  mandatory vaccination is not the route  that we have to follow we have to  convince the people we have to  make it understandable why vaccinations  are important however the situation is  getting worse we are understanding how  long a vaccination  is helpful probably just only for six  months we need the booster  vaccination  we we have the israeli data that shows  very clearly how important this third  job is and we have to get the vaccine  into the people right now and the  responsibility is very clear our health  care system is on the edge especially in  certain areas like saxony or or in  bavaria and that's where we have to show  responsibility and we cannot keep our  promises for a situation that got worse  now a member of the ethics council is  advising against compulsory vaccination  and has asked whether the government has  done enough to promote voluntary  vaccination  in your opinion has the government done  enough  no clearly the government didn't do  enough otherwise we would be in a  totally different situation today  again the third  vaccination the third [ __ ] it wasn't put  into place or was recommended  early enough despite the fact that  israel was doing that already and was  getting out of the way that they were  experiencing and now the new government  will probably be put in place this week  in our parliament and i'm pretty sure  that we are going to do this differently  and hopefully better so that we can in  front of the wave and not walking behind  the wave that's the only way that we can  get out of this c